1A|05 01 72|p. 19-8|transmitted RTTY text font color|
1A|05 01 73|00/01|RTTY log function|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 74|00/01|file saving format for the RTTY log|(00=Text, 01=HTML)
1A|05 01 75|00/01|RTTY time stamp set|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 76|00/01|RTTY Decode Log Time Stamp|(00=Local, 01=UTC)
1A|05 01 77|00/01|RTTY frequency stamp|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 78|00/01|scan speed|(00=Low, 01=High)
1A|05 01 79|00/01|scan resume|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 80|00/01|auto monitor function setting when transmitting a recorded voice memory|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 81|01/15|repeat interval to transmit recorded voice audio|(01=1 sec. to 15=15 sec.)
1A|05 01 82|00/01|recording mode for QSO recorder|(00=TX&RX, 01=RX Only)
1A|05 01 83|00/01|recording TX audio for QSO recorder|(00=Microphone audio, 01=TX monitor audio)
1A|05 01 84|00/01|squelch relation to recording RX audio for QSO recorder|(00=Always, 01=Squelch Auto)
1A|05 01 85|00/01|QSO record file split function setting|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 86|00/01|PTT Automatic Recording function setting|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 87|00 to 03|RX audio recording status for PTT Automatic Recording function|( 00=OFF (records no RX audio), 01=Records the RX audio just before 5 sec., 02=Records the RX audio just before 10 sec., 03=Records the RX audio just before 15 sec.)
1A|05 01 88|00 to 03|QSO PLAY Skip time|(00=3 sec., 01=5 sec., 02=10 sec., 03=30 sec.)
1A|05 01 89|00 to 09|NB depth|(00=1 to 09=10)
1A|05 01 90|0000 to 0255|NB width|(0000=1 to 0255=100)
1A|05 01 91|00 to 20|VOX delay|(00=0.0 sec. to 20=2.0 sec.)
1A|05 01 92|00 to 03|VOX voice delay|(00=OFF, 01=Short, 02=Mid., 03=Long)
1A|05 01 93|00/01|MF band attenuator setting|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|06|2 bytes: data mode 00/01 + filter 01~03|Send/read DATA mode setting|p.19-9; 00 data OFF (then filter also 00) 01 data ON
1A|07|1 byte 00/01|Send/read IP+ function setting|00 OFF 01 ON
1B|00|BCD 3 bytes|Send/read repeater tone frequency|p.19-11
1B|01|BCD 3 bytes|Set/read TSQL tone frequency|p.19-11
1C|00|1 byte 00/01|Send/read transceiver status (PTT)|00 RX 01 TX; auto-output on change when CI-V Output (for ANT) is ON
1C|01|1 byte 00~02|Send/read antenna tuner|00 OFF 01 ON 02 tuning (start / while tuning)
1C|02|1 byte 00/01|Send/read transmit frequency monitor|00 OFF 01 ON
1C|03|BCD 5 bytes frequency|Read transmit frequency|p.19-8
1C|04|1 byte 00/01|Send/read command to disable antenna controller output from REMOTE|
1E|00|none|Read number of available TX frequency bands|
1E|01|band edge data|Read TX band edge frequencies|p.19-8
1E|02|none|Read number of user-set TX frequency bands|
1E|03|band edge data|Send/read user-set TX band edge frequencies|p.19-8
21|00|BCD RIT frequency (p.19-11)|Send/read RIT frequency|
21|01|1 byte 00/01|Send/read RIT setting|00 OFF 01 ON
21|02|1 byte 00/01|Send/read TX (delta TX) setting|00 OFF 01 ON
25||1 byte 00/01 + BCD 5 bytes|Send/read selected or unselected VFO frequency|00 selected VFO, 01 unselected VFO; p.19-11
26||1 byte 00/01 + mode + data-mode 00/01 + filter 01~03|Send/read selected or unselected VFO operating mode and filter|00 selected 01 unselected; mode 00 LSB 01 USB 02 AM 03 CW 04 RTTY 05 FM 07 CW-R 08 RTTY-R; data and filter may be skipped; p.19-11
27|00|scope waveform data (p.19-12)|Read scope waveform data|only when 27 10 and 27 11 ON
27|10|1 byte 00/01|Send/read scope ON/OFF status|00 OFF 01 ON
27|11|1 byte 00/01|Send/read scope wave data output|00 OFF 01 ON; settable only when USB unlinked and CI-V baud 115200
27|12|1 byte 00|Send/read Main or Sub scope setting|00 = Main only
27|13|1 byte 00|Send/read Single/Dual scope setting|00 = Single only
27|14|1 byte 00/01|Send/read Scope Center mode or Fixed mode|00 center 01 fixed; p.19-12
27|15|BCD span data|Send/read span in Center mode|p.19-12
27|16|1 byte 01~03|Send/read edge number in Fixed mode|p.19-12
27|17|1 byte 00/01|Send/read scope hold|p.19-12
27|19|sign + level data|Send/read scope reference level|-20.0 dB..+20.0 dB in 0.5 dB steps; p.19-12
27|1A|1 byte 00~02|Send/read sweep speed|00 FAST 01 MID 02 SLOW; p.19-13
27|1B|1 byte 00/01|Send/read scope indication during TX in Center mode|00 OFF 01 ON
27|1C|1 byte 00~02|Send/read scope center frequency setting in Center mode|00 Filter center 01 Carrier point center 02 Carrier point center (Abs. Freq.)
27|1D|1 byte 00/01|Send/read scope VBW|00 Narrow 01 Wide; p.19-13
27|1E|edge frequency data|Send/read scope fixed edge frequencies|p.19-13
